From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:54:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Hold AOP messages in system
 sleep

The AOP's receive interrupt is IRQF_NO_SUSPEND, so each AOP message
wakes a CPU out of suspend-to-idle. On the J713 the AOP sends a report
every second (Aurora 7a3478e0bd, #831 measurements). Hold the AOP's
messages in its mailbox across suspend-to-idle instead of waking the
system, as the J713 does.

Nothing on the J604 needs an AOP message to wake it: the lid and the
power button come from the SMC, the keyboard and the trackpad from the
MTP, and the headphone jack from the CS42L84 interrupt. Only the
mailbox flag is set; it carries no J604 value.

The J604 AOP's message rate while asleep is TO-VERIFY (the interrupt
count of the AOP mailbox across one suspend-to-idle).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 53ed27cb74..c731686cfb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -808,6 +808,8 @@
 
 &aop_mbox {
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-AUD-3 */
+	/* A periodic report need not wake the system. */
+	apple,hold-rx-in-sleep;
 };
 
 &admac0 {
